Note: EPL DateTime Package — Usage Examples
Use "epl-datetime"

Note: --- Core ---
Create today equal to create_date(2026, 5, 13)
Print "Today:"
Print today

Print "Is 2024 a leap year?"
Print is_leap_year(2024)

Print "Days in February 2024:"
Print days_in_month(2024, 2)

Print "Is valid date 2023-02-29?"
Print is_valid_date(2023, 2, 29)

Note: --- Day of Week ---
Print "Day of week for 2026-05-13:"
Print day_of_week_name(2026, 5, 13)

Print "Day of year:"
Print day_of_year(2026, 5, 13)

Note: --- Arithmetic ---
Print "Add 30 days to today:"
Print add_days(today, 30)

Print "Subtract 100 days:"
Print subtract_days(today, 100)

Print "Add 3 months:"
Print add_months(today, 3)

Create christmas equal to create_date(2026, 12, 25)
Print "Days until Christmas:"
Print days_between(today, christmas)

Note: --- Formatting ---
Print format_date(today, "DD/MM/YYYY")
Print format_date(today, "YYYY-MM-DD")

Print "Month name:"
Print month_name(5)

Create past equal to create_date(2026, 4, 1)
Print "Relative:"
Print format_relative(past, today)

Note: --- Calendar ---
Print "May 2026 calendar:"
Print generate_calendar(2026, 5)

Note: --- Business Days ---
Create start equal to create_date(2026, 5, 1)
Create end_d equal to create_date(2026, 5, 31)
Print "Business days in May 2026:"
Print business_days_between(start, end_d)

Print "Quarter:"
Print quarter_of(today)
